translated_text:
Article 11

1. Services are implemented to fulfill the rights of women victims and are carried out with the following principles:
a. respect for human rights;
b. non-discrimination;
c. confidentiality;
d. empathy;
e. inclusion;
f. empowerment;
g. best interests of the victim;
h. honesty;
i. professionalism;
j. integration; and
k. sustainability.
2. Services to women victims must consider special conditions and needs based on the vulnerabilities experienced by women as referred to in Article 7.

